<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!-- Stops the status bar rendering as a cyan band above the title bar - the clash
         docs/decisions/06-mobile-ux.md left open.

         The record assumed the fix was "go edge-to-edge". Measured on API 36, the app is
         *already* edge-to-edge and always was: Android 15 forces it for anything targeting
         API 35 or later, so MAUI's `maui_edgetoedge_optout` attribute has nothing left to opt
         out of. Setting it to false was tried here and produced a pixel-identical screenshot.

         What actually paints the band is this style. MAUI gives the Shell's `AppBarLayout` a
         `?attr/colorPrimary` background, and under edge-to-edge that layout absorbs the status
         bar inset as padding and paints its own background through it. The Toolbar drawn
         inside it is white, from `Shell.BackgroundColor` - hence a cyan strip on top of a
         white bar rather than a uniformly cyan one. Matching the background to the Shell's is
         the whole fix; the insets were never mishandled.

         Parented off MAUI's own style so anything else it sets is inherited rather than
         forked, in the same way the theme override below the comment in Colors.xaml is. -->
    <style name="MauiAppBarLayout" parent="ThemeOverlay.AppCompat.Dark.ActionBar">
        <item name="android:background">@color/titleBarBackground</item>
    </style>

</resources>
